  "id": "Compound::DB00907 - Gene::1565",
  "verbalization": "Cocaine exhibits a strong binding interaction with Cyp2c8 and Cyp2c9, which are both involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid. This binding leads to the activation of arachidonic acid epoxygenase and monooxygenase activities, which are critical for the production of bioactive lipid mediators. These enzymatic activities are ultimately linked to the participation of Cyp2d6, suggesting a potential mechanism by which cocaine influences the expression or activity of Cyp2d6. The consistent evidence across multiple paths indicates that cocaine may modulate Cyp2d6 through the activation of arachidonic acid metabolism, potentially altering lipid signaling pathways. The observed scores suggest a robust and reliable relationship, supported by multiple independent pathways, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
